You must have the "Piper PA28-161 Warrior II" already installed. 

  You may find the original PA-28 161 Warrior II on "FGHangar". 
  
  In order to use the FGHangar to download free aircrafts, just go to the "Add-on" section 
  on the Startup screen and check the "Flightgear aircraft Distribution" option for your Flightgear version
  (2020.x or 2024.x at the moment of writing).

If you have the original "Piper PA-28 Warrior II already installed, you just need to copy and paste 
the new "PA28" folder inside your Flightgear's "Aicraft" directory; just replace the original texture
files with the new ones.

For example: 

   If you want to use the Terminal on Debian/Ubuntu Linux with Flightgear 2024.x
   you may use these commands:

        cd /tmp ;
        git clone https://github.com/ubuntuperonista/piper-warrior/ ;
        cd /tmp/piper-warrior/ ;
        mv Aircraft/PA28 /home/$USER/.fgfs/Aircraft/org.flightgear.fgaddon.stable_2024/
